    <string name="pdf_server">What the server keeps</string>
    <string name="pdf_server_sealed">Sealed on your phones, which the server stores but cannot read: practice sessions, counts, rounds and totals, targets and imported streak seeds. The keys stay on your devices.</string>
    <string name="pdf_server_encrypted">Kept encrypted in the server\'s database, readable by the running server: your display name and gender, your e-mail address, your username, linked sign-ins, the streaks you publish, the public keys of your account, devices and passkeys, push tokens and the text of reports you send.</string>
    <string name="pdf_server_plain">Kept as plain links between random numbers: that your account exists, who is friends with, invited, blocked, poked or reported whom, when things were written and how large each sealed record is. Cover photos never leave your phone.</string>

